problem statement

Develop a C++ program to represent communication towers as vertices and candidate communication links as weighted edges in a graph. Apply Kruskal’s algorithm to connect all communication towers at minimum total cost by constructing a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST). Display the selected links, their weights, the total cost, and the average weight of the selected links.
Suggested Modifications:
A) Modify the program to update the weight of an existing edge and reapply Kruskal’s algorithm to generate the updated Minimum Spanning Tree (MST).
B) Modify the program to display every selected edge along with its weight and the running total cost after each edge is added to the MST.
C) Modify the program to detect a disconnected graph and report whether a spanning tree can be formed. If the graph is disconnected, display an appropriate message indicating that a spanning tree cannot be formed.
